authors				Rick Caudill
status				testing

headline			SVG rendering library
description
	librsvg renders Scalable Vector Graphics (SVG) with cairo, and Pango for text. On Syllable it is built without GTK+: a small GdkPixbuf stand-in (gdk-pixbuf.c) provides the pixel buffers librsvg uses, and embedded raster images (<image>) are not loaded. Used by the SVG translator (system/sys/translators/svg).
licenses			LGPL-2

home				librsvg.sourceforge.net
locations			https://github.com/Rick-PyroOS/Syllable-Ports/raw/main/archives/

needs
	GLib >= 2.12
	Cairo >= 1.2
	Pango >= 1.10
	LibraryXML2 >= 2.4.7
	FontConfigure

; The archive is the 2008 Syllable port (librsvg-2.22.3.zip): no configure
; (it requires gdk-pixbuf-2.0); patches/Makefile builds the library.
configure-cmd		true
install-prefix-var	prefix

documentation
	README COPYING COPYING.LIB NEWS ChangeLog AUTHORS
